%Wrapper function for Newton's method
%   computes the projectile's position and targets position at given
%   (theta, t_c). The root of the function is where the projectile hits the
%   target.

% INPUTS:
%   x: 2-element column vector, x=[theta; t]
%       theta: firing angle of the projectile
%       t: time

%OUTPUTS:
%   f_out: a 2-element column vector, the (x,y) difference between the
%       target and projectiles positions at time t.Projectile hits ta
%    
function f_out = hit_target(x)
    theta = x(1);
    t = x(2);
    V_p = projectile_traj(theta, t);
    V_t = target_traj(t);

    f_out = V_p-V_t;
end

    